+// SA-nx: skipping a guest's busy-wait loops (the "idle-loop fast-forward" of
+// docs/runtime-interrupts.md, done per game rather than by the translator).
+//
+// A game that waits for an interrupt by calling an empty function over and over spends host time
+// running guest cycles in which nothing can change: everything that could end the wait is an
+// event at a time the scheduler already knows. When the empty function is called from one of the
+// named return addresses, the virtual clock jumps to the next event instead, which is what the
+// spinning would have reached. Kept out of abi.h on purpose: the translated code includes that,
+// and changing it rebuilds all of it.
